## Context

The author reviewed the local preview on 2026-09-24. This ticket holds the
cosmetic findings: wording, columns and labels, with no change to the site's
structure. The structural findings are in ticket 0956, which renames the
pages to the steps of `docs/jetp-language.md`. Where this ticket names the
page that is "Document rows" today, it uses 0956's name, **Lines**.

PR #1497 (ticket 0925, web-archive captures) is open and edits
`deliverables/jetp-observatory/app.js` on the Documents page: rebase on it
before starting.

## Documents page (D1)

1. The word "Collection" confuses readers. Rename it **"Fetch status"**, in
   the column header and in the filter box.
2. "Publisher's page —" appears on every row, which makes it noise. Show it
   only when there is a value.
3. In the same column, a document that was not collected must not carry a
   "Collected" date. Label that date **"Tried"**.
4. Put the document's **title** after its ID, in the same ID column.
5. Put the **size** in the Content type column and drop the size column.
6. Normalize the content-type string: one spelling per type, not a mix of
   MIME types and short labels.

## Lines page (D2, today "Document rows")

7. "Six selected document extracts" reads as if the reader had selected
   something. Say what the six are: the documents that publish a
   project-by-project table and whose tables are transcribed in full.
8. The CSV has no single "verbatim" field: each `raw_*` column is the
   publisher's own column, copied unchanged. Say so on the page and in the
   download's description, so a reader does not look for a quote column.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Items 1–6 are visible on the Documents page of the preview
- [ ] Items 7–8 are visible on the Lines page and on the CSV download
- [ ] `make check-fast` and the observatory's browser and render tests pass
